    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class with `@Test` methods, and it passes. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the generator step for `POST /api/owners`:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the owner's `city`\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of existing owners already in that city (`findAll()` filtered by city, case-insensitive). It still runs before `SaveOwner`, so the count excludes the owner being created.\n- Example: `LON-SMI-0007`.\n\n**Derived values rebuild automatically:** `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, built by concatenating `getCustomerCode()` \u2014 so it now yields e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26` with no code change needed.\n\n**Docs:** updated the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` descriptions and examples in `openapi.yml` to match the new format.\n\n**Tests:** the acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) now passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures).",
